[
    {
        "content": "<p>Hi all</p>\n<p>I am trying to make the addition notation work for some type <code>P R</code>, and I'm not sure whether I just don't get it or if there's an actual bug, but the behavior of the instance synthesis algorithm seems very weird to me.</p>\n<p>Instance synthesis for <code>HAdd X X X</code> succeeds normally when I have an instance of <code>Add X</code> using <code>instHadd</code>. But then if I register a second (unrelated) <code>HAdd</code> instance that can be attempted but will fail (e.g. <code>HAdd X X Prop</code>), then the whole search fails and the <code>instHadd</code> path isn't even attempted even though it would succeed. </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"c1\">--  lean v4.28.0</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">abbrev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- the issue disappear if this is changed to def</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">myadd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Add</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Add</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- when myHadd is not available instHAdd is correctly used to get HAdd (P R) (P R) (P R)</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">works1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Nonempty</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Add</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">myHadd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Nonempty</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">HAdd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- simple addition works as expected</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">works2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Add</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">--adding Nonempty triggers attempt to synthesize myHadd which fails *and* fails the whole search</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fails</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Nonempty</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Add</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- the parameterised HAdd instances are not helping</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Add</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">HAdd</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">add</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Add</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">HAdd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">instHAdd</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">failsAgain</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Nonempty</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Add</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- but with a specialised HAdd instantiation it's ok</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fixed</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Add</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">HAdd</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">add</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">works3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Nonempty</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Add</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Why does adding a new instance makes an already succeeding search fail? Why is the specialized <code>HAdd (P R) (P R) (P R)</code> instance needed when the normal parameterized <code>instHadd</code> should work ? <br>\nThanks !</p>",
        "id": 579943722,
        "sender_full_name": "Antoine Durand",
        "timestamp": 1773753903
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The third argument to <code>HAdd</code> is a <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=outParam#doc\">docs#outParam</a></p>",
        "id": 579944898,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1773754164
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This means when typeclass is looking for <code>HAdd (P R) (P R) (P R)</code>, it will instead look for <code>HAdd (P R) (P R) ?_</code>, and then check that what got filled in for <code>?_</code> matches <code>P R</code></p>",
        "id": 579945781,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1773754357
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>if it instead finds <code>HAdd (P R) (P R) Prop</code>, then it stops looking, and then <code>Prop</code> doesn't match <code>P R</code>, so it reports a failure</p>",
        "id": 579946020,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1773754405
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>But then shouldn't it backtrack and continue searching? If I enable tracing I can see that both instances are  candidates <code>#[@instHAdd, myHadd]</code>, yet it will stop at the first one. In general I don't expect synthesis to start failing if I add a random unrelated instance that is not meant to succeed.</p>",
        "id": 579957772,
        "sender_full_name": "Antoine Durand",
        "timestamp": 1773756784
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>For instance if I do this,</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nonempty</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inferInstanceAs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Nonempty</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Inhabited</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nonempty</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inferInstanceAs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Nonempty</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">synth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nonempty</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>then it works and I can see that <code>a</code> is attempted and fails, then <code>b</code> is attempted and succeeds. What is different here?</p>",
        "id": 579958284,
        "sender_full_name": "Antoine Durand",
        "timestamp": 1773756906
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><code>a</code> has an <em>assumption</em> <code>[Inhabited A]</code>. When trying to use <code>a</code>, Lean checks if it knows that the assumption is satisfied, realizes that it doesn't know that, so it can't apply <code>a</code>. Then it tries <code>b</code>.</p>",
        "id": 579958945,
        "sender_full_name": "Sébastien Gouëzel",
        "timestamp": 1773757055
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>For your original question, you should note that the third parameter to <code>HAdd</code> is an outparam. There should never be two instances of the form <code>HAdd A A B</code> and <code>HAdd A A C</code> because of the definition of outparams: it should be determined uniquely by the other parameters (here <code>A</code>, <code>A</code>)</p>",
        "id": 579959702,
        "sender_full_name": "Sébastien Gouëzel",
        "timestamp": 1773757215
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ok I think I understand better now, many thanks !</p>",
        "id": 579964508,
        "sender_full_name": "Antoine Durand",
        "timestamp": 1773758261
    }
]